===Etymology===
From {{af|en|testis|alt1=test(is)|-o-|-sterone|t3=steroid hormone}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/tɛˈstɒ.stə.ɹəʊn/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-testosterone.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/tɛˈstɑ.stəˌɹoʊn/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|steroid hormone}} A {{w|steroid hormone}} that stimulates [[development]] of [[male]] {{w|secondary sexual characteristic}}s, produced mainly in the [[testis|testes]], but also in the [[ovary|ovaries]] and [[adrenal cortex]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=[[w:Bill Bryson|Bill Bryson]]|title=The Body: A Guide for Occupants|publisher=Black Swan (2020)|page=168|passage=Mammalian testes contain almost no '''testosterone''' because it is sent out into the body as quickly as it is made.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} [[manly|Manly]] behavior, often of an [[aggressive]] or foolishly [[reckless]] nature.
#: {{ux|en|Mother encouraged James to rely more on intelligence and less on '''testosterone''' to deal with the neighbor's son.}}

